{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s39-p01",
      "text": "As a country powerful in maths, China has many creative folk games full of maths wisdom.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p02",
      "text": "You may play them during a sunny afternoon or on a vacation abroad.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p03",
      "text": "Let's take a look at three of them.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p04",
      "text": "Chinese Nine Linked Rings Puzzle",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p05",
      "text": "It's believed that the Nine Linked Rings puzzle was created in the Western Han Dynasty and may have been played even by the emperor himself.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p06",
      "text": "It is usually made up of nine rings connected to a handle.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p07",
      "text": "Players have to remove all the rings from the handle to win the game.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p08",
      "text": "This is not a simple game.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p09",
      "text": "The solution takes 341 moves.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p10",
      "text": "So lots of effort is required.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p11",
      "text": "But if you learn to solve it, you'll probably never forget.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p12",
      "text": "Tangram",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p13",
      "text": "The tangram is a puzzle made up of seven pieces of different shapes, including a square, a parallelogram, and five triangles.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p14",
      "text": "Players need to use all the pieces to make a shape.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p15",
      "text": "In the 18th century, the tangram was brought to the West and soon gathered international attention.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p16",
      "text": "Today, you can play it on a computer screen or over the Internet.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p17",
      "text": "Luban Lock",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p18-01",
      "text": "It is said that the Luban Lock was first created by Lu Ban,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p18-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p18-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p18-02",
      "text": "who was a famous engineer in ancient China.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p18-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p18-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p19",
      "text": "The lock has a lot to do with solid geometry.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p20",
      "text": "It's hard to separate the six pieces.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p21",
      "text": "However, it is usually easier to unlock a Luban lock than to fix it back together.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s39-p22",
      "text": "Many people like to collect different kinds of Luban locks, considering them as treasures of Chinese culture.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s39-p22.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
